{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments","title":"def:has-min-segments","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":39,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#def:has-min-segments","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"def:has-min-segments","line":48,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Spaces with minimizing segments]\n\\label{def:has-min-segments}\n\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\n\n\nA metric space $(M,d)$ \\emph{has minimizing segments} if every $x,y\\in M$\nare joined by a unit-speed minimizing map\n$\\sigma\\colon[0,d(x,y)]\\to M$ with $\\sigma(0)=x$ and\n$\\sigma(d(x,y))=y$. A metric space is \\emph{proper} when its\nclosed balls are compact. Connected complete Riemannian manifolds have both\nproperties by Lemmas~\\ref{lem:minimizing-segment-exists}\nand~\\ref{lem:ends-exist}.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Spaces with minimizing segments] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6861732d6d696e2d7365676d656e7473\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aminimizing-geodesic-window\">↗ def:minimizing-geodesic-window</a> <p></p>A metric space <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,d)$\">$(M,d)$</span> <em>has minimizing segments</em> if every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x,y\\in M$\">$x,y\\in M$</span> are joined by a unit-speed minimizing map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sigma \\colon [0,d(x,y)]\\to M$\">$\\sigma \\colon [0,d(x,y)]\\to M$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sigma (0)=x$\">$\\sigma (0)=x$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sigma (d(x,y))=y$\">$\\sigma (d(x,y))=y$</span>. A metric space is <em>proper</em> when its closed balls are compact. Connected complete Riemannian manifolds have both properties by Lemmas <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aminimizing-segment-exists\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:minimizing-segment-exists\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6d696e696d697a696e672d7365676d656e742d657869737473\">2</a> and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aends-exist\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ends-exist\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a656e64732d6578697374\">2</a>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ray-exists-metric","title":"lem:ray-exists-metric","label":"lem:ray-exists-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:line-exists-metric","title":"lem:line-exists-metric","label":"lem:line-exists-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#ends","title":"ends","label":"ends"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","title":"lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","label":"lem:asymptotic-ray-exists"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments","title":"def:has-min-segments","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Spaces with minimizing segments]\n\\label{def:has-min-segments}\n\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\n\n\nA metric space $(M,d)$ \\emph{has minimizing segments} if every $x,y\\in M$\nare joined by a unit-speed minimizing map\n$\\sigma\\colon[0,d(x,y)]\\to M$ with $\\sigma(0)=x$ and\n$\\sigma(d(x,y))=y$. A metric space is \\emph{proper} when its\nclosed balls are compact. Connected complete Riemannian manifolds have both\nproperties by Lemmas~\\ref{lem:minimizing-segment-exists}\nand~\\ref{lem:ends-exist}.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}